  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.55 & =0.35+P(B)-0.15 \\\\ P(B) & =0.55+0.15-0.35 \\\\  & =0.35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{\u2032}\\cap {B}^{\u2032}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/eba791c99c1b4706275f353ca221cdad5e535b508e57346e28fa18a372a080ee.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{\u2032}\\cap {B}^{\u2032})=0.45.\n$$",
